# Local modifications used to produce these outputs (standalone GPU box, 4x H200, 2026-09-15). Not committed anywhere.
# Repo kaleybrauer/filler-token-reasoning @ c2df06b; environment per QWEN35_GPU_RUNBOOK.md step 1 except item 4.
#
# 1. extract_qwen35_states.py step_concepts (concepts + templates): torch.stack over layers that live on different GPUs
#    (device_map="auto") raised "Expected all tensors to be on the same device". Each layer's state is now moved to one
#    GPU before stacking; the fp16 conversion still happens on GPU, values unchanged. Applied before 122B concepts
#    (122B unembed + paragraphs were produced by the unmodified script) and for all of 397B.
# 2. extract_qwen35_states.py step_unembed: G-UNEMBED additionally compares the offline readout with an fp32
#    recomputation through the model's own final norm and lm_head ("fp32_reference" in check.json). Pass if either
#    the bf16 comparison (original keys, "bf16_passed") or the fp32 one has top-1 1.0 and corr > 0.999 ("passed_via").
#    397B: bf16 top-1 0.875 (probe 207: fp32 top-2 ' no' 16.328 vs ' the' 16.311, both 16.375 in bf16, argmax tie),
#    fp32_reference top-1 1.0, corr 1.0, max_abs 3e-5 -> passed via fp32_reference. 122B check.json predates this
#    change (passed on bf16). Approved by Kaley before the 397B rerun.
# 3. transformers 5.16.1 quantizers/quantizer_finegrained_fp8.py update_tp_plan: FP8Experts._impl_tp_layer_overrides
#    .get(impl) returns None for any impl but deepgemm_megamoe, so every Qwen3-family FP8 load raised
#    AttributeError: 'NoneType' object has no attribute 'get'. Fixed with "or {}" (identity; the TP plan is unused
#    in a single-process device_map load).
# 4. kernels: the unpinned "uv pip install kernels" gave 0.17.0, but transformers 5.16.1 accepts >=0.16.0,<0.17.0 and
#    needs it for the kernels-community/finegrained-fp8 Triton kernel (the only FP8 path when the model spans several
#    GPUs); with 0.17.0 every FP8 forward raises ImportError. Pinned kernels==0.16.2 (+ kernels-data==0.16.2) after
#    the 122B run. No effect on bf16 compute: hub layer kernels apply only with use_kernels=True; fla/causal_conv1d
#    are not installed, so the linear-attention layers ran the torch path in both models.
#
